 "written": "2026-10-17, after reading the distinct record texts of the two new cards (all 335 BIA land area names; the 9 WRC community texts) and searching the 16-card corpus for tribal and fire words (one PAD-US unit is designated Native American Land Area). No query was embedded or scored on the 18-card corpus before this file was hashed, v2's included.",
 "changes_from_v2": [
  "keeps every v2 query unchanged (95: 21 collection, 48 value, 26 control)",
  "adds c22-c26 (collection) and v49-v63 (value) for bia-lar and wrc-communities",
  "adds controls n29-n39, next to the new cards on purpose: tribal and fire subjects with no record loaded; with v2's 26 that is 37",
  "no v2 control becomes relevant: n03 'wildfire perimeters' stays a control (see disputable)"
 ],
 "disputable": [
  "v32 'level 1 trauma center' counts LEVEL I and LEVEL I PEDIATRIC; LEVEL II-IV and the state codes (CTH, TRF, RTC, ATH) are partial",
  "v39 'elementary schools' counts only school level Elementary, not Prekindergarten",
  "v40 'high schools' counts High and Secondary",
  "v42 'online virtual school' counts Full Virtual and 'Virtual with face to face options'",
  "v46 'rural schools' counts NCES locale codes 41-43 (Rural: Fringe, Distant, Remote) only, not Town",
  "v48 'schools in New Mexico': the record text says 'state: NM', an abbreviation",
  "n22 'colleges and universities' is a control: the NCES layer is K-12 only",
  "n28 'emergency shelters' is a control: hospitals are not shelters",
  "n03 'wildfire perimeters' stays a control: WRC community records are modelled risk ranks of Census places, not fire perimeters",
  "c22-c24 count the one PAD-US unit designated 'Native American Land Area' as relevant, as well as every BIA land area",
  "v52 'Apache reservations' counts San Carlos (the San Carlos Apache reservation), whose BIA name does not say Apache",
  "v54 'Seminole reservations in Florida' counts the Seminole Tribe of Florida's six land areas (Big Cypress, Brighton, Hollywood (Dania), Immokalee, Fort Pierce, Tampa); Miccosukee is partial",
  "v55 'pueblos in New Mexico' counts the 19 New Mexico pueblos by their BIA names (San Juan is Ohkay Owingeh), plus Acoma (Red Lake); Ysleta Del Sur (a Texas pueblo) is partial",
  "v59 'Paiute reservations' counts only the two land areas whose BIA name says Paiute; the many Paiute colonies and reservations named otherwise (Bishop, Pyramid Lake, Walker River and others) are partial",
  "v62 counts the WRC records whose exclusion reason starts 'no people'",
  "n32 'Census tribal statistical areas' is a control: BIA's layer is trust land, and the card says Census areas are not this",
  "n34 'Indian Health Service clinics' is a control: hospital record text carries no owner, and a clinic is not a hospital"
 ],
